Drops the customer_entity join from every mst_rewards_transaction collection and adds it back only where the grid actually needs it
Original JIRA ticket: IPET-2843
IPET-3635: the join moved from _initSelect() into joinCustomerName() instead of being removed outright - the legacy grid behind the transactions CSV/XML export calls joinCustomerName() and then joinCustomerGroup(), which joins ON customer.group_id, so without the customer alias the export query failed with "Unknown column 'customer.group_id' in 'on clause'"
Coupled with render-expired-points-comment-in-customer-locale.patch: that patch adds its own joinLeft on the same `customer` alias inside Cron::expirePoints(), which only works while _initSelect() does not. Reverting this patch requires adjusting that one in the same change.

